The paper deals with finding solutions to a specific inhomogeneous Kirchhoff type elliptic PDE given by

$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\displaystyle
\left(\phi(\tau)\right)(t) \Delta_{\mathbb{S}^{n-1}}u=\left|u^{2^{*}(t)}\right|^{4/n}u^{s(t)}\text{ in }\mathbb{S}^{n-1},
\text{ $\tau\in\mathbb{R}$, $s(t)\in C^0([0,1])$, $s(t)\leq2^{*}(t)=\frac{2(n-s)}{n-2}$,}
\end{array}
\right.
$$

where $\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$ denotes the unit sphere in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$. A novel approach is developed to tackle this problem by means of a new singular Trudinger-Moser inequality when the Moser-Trudinger inequality develops singularities. As a result, several new solutions can be obtained for a specific Kirchhoff type elliptic PDE under certain conditions.

